comment_body:
I do not like this approach because we are still supporting violation of Dependency Inversion principle.
In current place Shopcart depends on it's children classes.
In any time we will add new child in hierarchy, we will be forced to change our abstract class.

I think it will be better to use constant \Magento\Backend\App\AbstractAction::ADMIN_RESOURCE and override it in each child.

E.g. 
\Magento\Reports\Controller\Adminhtml\Report\Shopcart::ADMIN_RESOURCE = 'Magento_Reports::shopcart';
\Magento\Reports\Controller\Adminhtml\Report\Shopcart\Product::ADMIN_RESOURCE = 'Magento_Reports::product';
\Magento\Reports\Controller\Adminhtml\Report\Shopcart\Customer::ADMIN_RESOURCE = null;
Etc.

